-- title:
--   Hecke and Pi translates of even rigidifications preserve levels
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $r$ and $\bar r$ are primes with $\bar r \neq r$ and $N$ is a nonzero natural number with $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree (`hrr`, `hrN`, `hrbarN`, `hN`).
--
--   **Base rings.** $\mathcal O$ is a characteristic‑zero domain which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), $\pi \in \mathcal O$ is irreducible (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ is $(\pi)$‑adically complete (`hcomplete`), the residue ring $\mathcal O/(\pi)$ has exactly $r$ elements (`hres`), and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ is a characteristic‑zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Next, $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ (written `Onr`) is a characteristic‑zero domain and $\mathcal O$‑algebra carrying an $\mathcal O$‑algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`); moreover every element of `Onr` satisfies some monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $(\pi)$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial over `Onr` of positive degree has a root modulo $(\pi)$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod{(\pi)}$ for all $x$ (`hFr`). Finally $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (multiplicatively written) is a homomorphism which, by `hvdet`, sends $g$ to $n$ exactly when $\det g = u\,\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^{\times}$; thus $\mathrm{vdet}$ is the $\pi$‑adic valuation of the determinant. For $k \in \mathbb Z$ and $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ an $\mathcal O$‑algebra map, `frobTwist Onr Fr k ψ` is $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$; below $v(\det g)$ abbreviates `Multiplicative.toAdd (vdet g)`.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli schemes.** $a, b \in \mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a, b]$ is indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), and $\Lambda$ is a maximal $\mathbb Z$‑order in it (`hΛ`). The scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$, with structure morphism $f$ and point map `pt` assigning to each ring $S$, each $S$‑point of $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ and each fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$‑action and level‑$N$ structure over $S$ a point of $\mathcal X$, is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒳`). Further, $n \geq 3$ with $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $\gcd(n, N) = 1$ (`hn`, `hrn`, `hrbarn`, `hnN`); $M$ with $f_M$ and `ptF` is a fine moduli scheme for curves with full level‑$n$ structure (`hM`); a group $G$ acts on $M$ by automorphisms $\rho$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ in the sense of `IsLevelTwistAction` (`hρ`); and $p : M \to \mathcal X$ is the forgetful morphism, compatible with the base (`hp`), $G$‑invariant (`hρp`) and compatible with the point maps (`hp_pt`).
--
--   **Hecke tower and Atkin–Lehner maps on $\mathcal X$.** For each prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$, $\mathcal Y_\ell$ with $g_\ell$ and `ptT` is a coarse moduli space for curves with an extra level‑$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), and $d_0, d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ lie over $f$ (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`), $d_0$ forgetting the extra structure (`hd₀`) and $d_1$ sending a pair $(E, K)$ to the target of a level‑$\ell$ isogeny out of it (`hd₁`). The endomorphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r}$ of $\mathcal X$ lie over $f$ (`harf`, `harbarf`) and realise the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** $a_1, b_1 \in \mathbb Q$ are such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ is definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`); $\Lambda_1$ is a maximal order, $R_1 \leq \Lambda_1$ an Eichler order of level $N$ (`hΛ₁`, `hR₁`, `hRΛ₁`); $n_1$ is a finite idele in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that `meetOrder R₁ n₁` is an Eichler order of level $N r$ (`hS₁`); $\iota_0$ is an injective $\mathbb Q$‑algebra embedding of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ into $M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`); $v$ is a height‑one prime of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$ (`hv`). The group $\Gamma^{t}$ (`Γt`) is the group of units integral away from $v$ for $R_1$ (`hΓt`). For each prime $\ell \notin \{r, \bar r\}$ elements $s_\ell$ and finite ideles $s^{f}_\ell$ are given, and `hs` requires (four clauses): $s^{f}_\ell$ has component $s_\ell$ at every place not above $r$ and component $1$ at places above $r$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $(s^{f}_\ell)^{-1}$ lies in `levelHeckeUSet Λ₁ (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` when $\ell \mid N$ and in `primeHeckeSet (meetOrder R₁ n₁) ℓ` otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$; $\Gamma^{t}_{\ell}$ is $\Gamma^{t} \cap s_\ell \Gamma^{t} s_\ell^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`). An element $\bar w$ with $\mathrm{nrd}(\bar w) = \bar r$ normalising $\Gamma^{t}$ is fixed (`hwbar`).
--
--   **Reduction data and uniformisation hypotheses.** All integers lie in $\Lambda$ (`hΛℤ`), and `coord` is a coordinate map $\Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{r^2}^{\,2}$ in the sense of `IsOrderCoord` (`hcoord`). Over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ there are: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$‑module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), two‑dimensional formal coordinates $\theta_0$ on $A_0$ exhibiting $A_0$ as a formal module via `coord`, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`), families $e, e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma^{t}$ with $e_\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees `deg`. The hypotheses `hE1`, `hE1mul`, `hE1sc`, `hE1'`, `hE2`, `hE3`, `hE4` (summarised here) require: $(e_\gamma, e'_\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg \gamma}$ preserving level; multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e_\gamma$ up to multiplication by $r$‑powers; $e_\gamma$ is multiplication by $c$ up to $r$‑powers when $\gamma$ is the scalar $c$, and conversely $e_\gamma$ scalar up to $r$‑powers forces $\gamma$ scalar; for every injective ring map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\mathbb Z_{r^2}$‑action and of $\varpi$ on $X_0$ into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e_\gamma$ is induced on formal coordinates by a centraliser element $\varepsilon$ with $E_0(\varepsilon) = r^{k_\gamma}\, g\, \iota_0(\gamma)\, g^{-1}$; each full level‑$n$ structure on $A_0$ gets a label map $\Gamma^{t} \to \Lambda$, multiplicative modulo $n$ and sending scalars to scalars modulo $n$; and every $r$‑power isogeny preserving level of a curve over an algebraically closed field pulled back from $A_0$ comes, up to $r$‑powers, from some $e_\gamma$. In addition an order $R_2 \leq R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$‑power denominators relative to $R_1$ (`hR₂r`) is given together with endomorphisms $\hat e_x$ of $A_0$ over the base (`hê`), and `hE5a`, `hE5b1`, `hE5b2`, `hE5b3`, `hE5c`, `hE5d`, `hE5e` (summarised here) require that $\hat e$ is additive, commutes with the $\Lambda$‑action and preserves level, that $\hat e_1 = \mathrm{id}$, $\hat e_{xy} = \hat e_y \circ \hat e_x$, $\hat e_m$ is multiplication by $m$ for $m \in \mathbb Z$, $\hat e_{\bar x} \circ \hat e_x$ is multiplication by $\mathrm{nrd}(x)$, that $\hat e_x$ agrees with $e_\gamma$ up to $r$‑powers when $x = r^{k}\gamma$, and that a single $g$ as in `hE2` simultaneously linearises all $e_\gamma$ and all $\hat e_x$.
--
--   **Formal side and Drinfeld dictionary.** A ring map $\iota : \mathbb Z_{r^2} \to O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ is given, together with a formal $\mathcal O_D$‑module $\Phi$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); `MD` is a moduli package for $r$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and $\eta$ assigns to each rigidified object over a ring in which $r$ is nilpotent a point of `MD`. The hypothesis `hη` has three clauses: $\eta$ is injective on admissible objects up to `Rigidified.IsIsomorphic`, it is natural in the base, and every point of `MD` is, locally on a finite cover of the base by principal opens, of the form $\eta(t)$ for an admissible $t$. The map $E_0$ from the centraliser of the action endomorphisms and of $\varpi_\Phi$ into $M_2(K_0)$ is injective and, for a suitable $m$, its image contains $r^{m} M_2(\mathcal O)$ and satisfies $r^{m} E_0(e) \in M_2(\mathcal O)$ for all $e$ (`hE₀`). The transformation `eD` compares the functor of `GPoint`s of `MD` on noetherian $\mathcal O$‑algebras $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent to the product of the functor of $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$‑points and Deligne's functor $\Omega$ of $\pi$‑adic lattice data, and `hnatD`, `hbijD`, `hfstD`, `hGLD`, `hPiD`, `hPiexD` require respectively: naturality, bijectivity, that the first component of `eD x` is the structure leg of $x$, that `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy ι Φ η Fr E₀ g` corresponds under `eD` to `OmegaNr.IsTwistedAct π Onr Fr vdet B g` (for $(\psi, P)$ and $(\psi', P')$ the latter means $\psi' = \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g)}$ together with $P'$ being the $g^{-1}$‑pullback of $P$ in the sense of `DeligneDatum.IsPullback`), that a $\Pi$‑translate (`ModuliPackage.G.IsPiTranslate ι Φ η Fr`) is sent to the pair consisting of the first Frobenius twist of the leg and the unchanged lattice datum, and that $\Pi$‑translates always exist. Here `ModuliPackage.G.IsActBy ι Φ η Fr E₀ g x x'` asserts the existence of a centraliser element $e$ and of $k, m'$ with $E_0(e) = r^{k} g^{-1}$, with kernel of degree $r^{2m'}$, such that $x'$ is the translate of $x$ by $e$ in the sense of `ModuliPackage.G.IsTranslate` (legs differing by the Frobenius twist $m' - 2k$, and the underlying rigidified objects locally related by `Rigidified.IsTranslate`). Finally $\kappa$ relates $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(\pi)$ to $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatibly with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and $\beta_0$ is an isogeny from $\Phi$ to the base change of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ of height $4 n_0$ (`hβ₀`).
--
--   **Base point data.** $P_0$ is a full level‑$n$ structure on $A_0$. An Atkin–Lehner quotient of $A_0$ at $\bar r$ is given by $A_{0w}$ with $a_w, a_w'$ (`hALw`), together with an isogeny pair $b_w, b_w'$ of degree $r^{k_w}$ from $A_{0w}$ to $A_0$ (`hBSw`) with $b_w$ preserving level (`hBSwlev`); `hJOINTw` strengthens `hE2` by requiring that for each injective $E_0$ a single $g$ linearises all $e_\gamma$ as $r^{k_\gamma} g \iota_0(\gamma) g^{-1}$ and also provides a centraliser element $\varepsilon_w$ inducing $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ on formal coordinates with $E_0(\varepsilon_w) = r^{k_w} g\, \iota_0(\bar w)\, g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The dictionary $\Xi$.** For each noetherian $\mathcal O$‑algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, each $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal O} B$ and each rigidified curve over $(B, \psi)$ — that is, a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ together with a `Rigidification`: curves $E_b$ and $A_b$ over $B/(\pi)$ pulled back from $E$ and from $A_0$ along the residue leg of $\psi$, and an $r^{d}$‑isogeny $\varphi : E_b \to A_b$ preserving level — $\Xi$ produces a `GPoint` of `MD` over $B$. Its properties are: `hΞleg`, that over a $B$ with no nontrivial idempotents the structure leg of $\Xi$ is $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{k}$ for some $k \in \mathbb Z$; `hΞnat`, compatibility with base change along $\mathcal O$‑algebra maps when the rigidifications correspond; `hΞiso`, invariance of $\Xi$ under isomorphisms of the underlying curves whose rigidification data are comparable in the displayed sense (up to multiplication by $r$‑powers); and `hΞdef`, the defining formula: for connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent and a rigidified curve whose underlying curve is a formal module via `coord`, $X$, $\theta$, there are $j \leq 1$ and a rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, with $\theta$ transported from $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ and the given rigidification at level $j$ (`IsRigTransport`), admissible for $\iota$ and $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$, such that $\Xi$ of the curve equals the point with leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-j}$ and underlying point $\eta(t)$. A matrix $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ is fixed, and two equivariance hypotheses are assumed: `heqΓ`, that over connected $B$, if $\rho'$ is the translate of $\rho$ by $e_\gamma$ in the sense of `Rigidification.IsTranslateBy`, then for some $c \in \mathbb Z$ the images $\Xi\langle E, \rho\rangle$ and $\Xi\langle E, \rho'\rangle$ are related by `IsActBy` for the matrix $Z^{c}\,(g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1})$, where $Z$ denotes the central unit $r \cdot 1$; and `heqW`, the analogous statement with $\bar w$ in place of $\gamma$ for an Atkin–Lehner quotient $q$, $q'$ at $\bar r$ over a connected $B$ in which $\bar r$ is invertible, under the displayed comparison of the two rigidifications through $a_w$ followed by $b_w$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\tilde\psi := \psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}$. Two statements are asserted.
--
--   (1) For every noetherian $\mathcal O$‑algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent (`hB`) in which every idempotent is $0$ or $1$ (`hconn`), every $\psi : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal O} B$, every lattice datum $P \in \Omega(B)$, every fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ and every rigidification $\varrho$ of $E$ relative to $\tilde\psi$ such that the leg of $\Xi_B \tilde\psi \langle E, \varrho\rangle$ is exactly $\tilde\psi$ (evenness) and `eD` of $\Xi_B \tilde\psi \langle E, \varrho\rangle$ is carried to $(\psi, P)$ by the $g_0^{-1}$‑twisted action: for every further curve $E'$ with rigidification $\varrho'$ relative to $\tilde\psi$, every unit $h$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ and every $c \in \mathbb Z$ such that $\Xi_B \tilde\psi \langle E', \varrho'\rangle$ is the `IsActBy`‑image of $\Xi_B \tilde\psi \langle E, \varrho\rangle$ under $Z^{c}\,(g_0\,\iota_0(h)\,g_0^{-1})$, and for every $\psi''$ and $P''$ with $(\psi'', P'')$ the $\iota_0(h)$‑twisted translate of $(\psi, P)$, there exists a rigidification $\varrho''$ of the same curve $E'$ relative to $\psi'' \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}$ such that:
--
--   (1a) the leg of $\Xi_B (\psi'' \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}) \langle E', \varrho''\rangle$ equals $\psi'' \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}$;
--
--   (1b) `eD` of that point is carried to $(\psi'', P'')$ by the $g_0^{-1}$‑twisted action;
--
--   (1c) $\varrho'$ and $\varrho''$ transport extra level structures identically: for every prime $\ell \neq r$ which is invertible in $B$, every extra level‑$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ (the Lean binder here reuses the name `K₀`) and every two extra level‑$\ell$ structures $C$, $C'$ on $E'$, if every point of $\varrho'.E_b$ over a $B/(\pi)$‑scheme whose image under $\varrho'.g_b$ factors through $C$ has its image under $\varrho'.\varphi$ followed by $\varrho'.g_A$ factoring through the given structure on $A_0$, and the same holds for $\varrho''$ and $C'$, then for every $B$‑scheme $T$ and every point $R$ of $E'$ over $T$, $R$ factors through $C$ if and only if it factors through $C'$;
--
--   (1d) the height‑normalised full level‑$n$ structures differ by $r^{c}$: for all $P_n, P_n''$ full level‑$n$ structures on $E'$, if $P_n$ is the norm‑level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho'$ and $P_n''$ the norm‑level transport of $P_0$ along $\varrho''$, both in the sense of `Rigidification.IsNormLevelTransport Fr θ₀ κ β₀ Φ ι coord P₀`, then $r^{(-c)^{+}} \cdot P_n'' = r^{c^{+}} \cdot P_n$ as points of $E'$ for the group law of $E'$ over the identity, where $x^{+}$ denotes `Int.toNat`.
--
--   (2) With the same hypotheses on $B$, `hconn`, $\psi$, $P$, $E$ and the even rigidification $\varrho$ relative to $\tilde\psi$ with image $(\psi, P)$: for every curve $E'$, every $\psi_1 : O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to_{\mathcal O} B$, every rigidification $\varrho'$ of $E'$ relative to $\psi_1$, every $c \in \mathbb Z$ and every `GPoint` $y$ over $B$ such that $y$ is a $\Pi$‑translate of $\Xi_B \tilde\psi\langle E, \varrho\rangle$ and $\Xi_B \psi_1 \langle E', \varrho'\rangle$ is the `IsActBy`‑image of $y$ under the central matrix $Z^{c}$, there exists a rigidification $\varrho''$ of $E'$ relative to $(\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}) \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-v(\det g_0)}$ such that the leg of $\Xi_B$ of $\langle E', \varrho''\rangle$ at that base point equals it, `eD` of that point is carried by the $g_0^{-1}$‑twisted action to $(\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}, P)$, and the same height‑normalised level relation as in (1d) holds: for all $P_n, P_n''$ transported from $P_0$ along $\varrho'$ and $\varrho''$ respectively, $r^{(-c)^{+}} \cdot P_n'' = r^{c^{+}} \cdot P_n$. No extra‑level clause is asserted in (2).
--
--   This is an equivariance step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld $p$-adic uniformisation of the Shimura curve attached to an indefinite quaternion algebra ramified at $r$ and $\bar r$: it says that the dictionary between rigidified fake elliptic curves in characteristic‑$r$ deformation theory and Drinfeld's special formal modules, read through the lattice‑datum description of the $\pi$-adic upper half plane, carries Hecke translates by units of the definite quaternion algebra and the $\Pi$-translation back to rigidifications of the translated curve, keeping track both of the transported extra level structures and of the height‑normalised full level‑$n$ structure. It is used in the construction of the translation and level comparison [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.exists_translate_level_eq_of_levelHom_of_character_of_isTwistedAct_heightNormalised_eq`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.Rigidification.exists_translate_level_eq_of_levelHom_of_character_of_isTwistedAct_heightNormalised_eq).
